- **Citation_focus_text**: *"Following the setup introduced by Du et al. (2023)"* (this is the explicit reference to prior work).
- **Analysis**: The rest of the paragraph describes a standard protocol (common in ML literature), not novel contributions. The citation is the only reference to prior work.
- **Result**:  
  - Technical percentage: **20** (minimal new description)  
  - Citation percentage: **80** (most of the value comes from referencing existing work)

#### Example 2: A Methods Paragraph Describing a New Approach
**Text**:  
*"We explore inference-time strategies to address the challenge of real-time decision-making. This approach involves dynamically adjusting model parameters during inference, which has not been used in prior work. Drawing inspiration from Khan et al. (2022), we implement a novel optimization layer that reduces latency by 40%."*

- **Citation_focus_text**: *"Drawing inspiration from Khan et al. (2022)"* (this is the explicit reference).
- **Analysis**: The rest of the paragraph describes a new method (dynamic parameter adjustment) with quantifiable results (40% latency reduction). The citation is minimal (only for inspiration).
- **Result**:  
  - Technical percentage: **90** (most value is original contribution)  
  - Citation percentage: **10** (only a small part references prior work)

